      "instruction": "Verification feedback:\nVerification complete. Findings saved to `review.md`.\n\n**Evidence gathered (implementation untouched, sha256 `1ede7a44…94d4f`):**\n\n| Command | Exit | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `node review_add_test.mjs` | 1 | `AssertionError: -1 !== 5` on `add(2, 3)` |\n| `node review_add_matrix.mjs` | 1 | 5 of 7 cases FAIL (`total=7 failures=5`) |\n| `node review_proposed_patch_check.mjs` | 0 | proposed `a + b` satisfies all cases |\n\n```\nFAIL\tpositive\tadd(2, 3) => -1\texpected 5\nFAIL\tpositive-float\tadd(0.1, 0.2) => -0.1\texpected 0.30000000000000004\nFAIL\tnegative\tadd(-2, -3) => 1\texpected -5\nFAIL\tmixed\tadd(-7, 4) => -11\texpected -3\nPASS\tzero-zero\tadd(0, 0) => 0\texpected 0\nPASS\tzero-right\tadd(5, 0) => 5\texpected 5\nFAIL\tzero-left\tadd(0, -5) => 5\texpected -5\n```\n\n**Defect:** the named ESM export `add(a, b)` exists and returns a `number`, but the body computes `a - b` (subtraction). The two passing zero cases are accidental (`x - 0 === x`).\n\n**Required correction in `calculator.js`:** change the operator in the return expression from `-` to `+`, i.e.\n`export function add(a, b) { return a + b; }` — keeping the same signature, param names/order, and module format. Then both review scripts must exit 0 with `failures=0`.\n\n<REVISE>",
